<TrustPage
  title="Contact Havemoon"
  description="Contact status for editorial corrections, source questions, privacy requests, and future business inquiries."
>
  <h2>Contact status</h2>
  <p class="trust-note">
    <strong>Local preview:</strong> a verified public email address has not yet been supplied. Havemoon
    will not publish a placeholder address, borrowed identity, or contact channel that the operator cannot
    monitor.
  </p>

  <h2>Channels planned for public launch</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Editorial corrections and source questions</li>
    <li>Privacy and data requests</li>
    <li>Technical problems with calculators or site access</li>
    <li>Clearly separated business and service inquiries</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What to include</h2>
  <p>
    For a content question, include the page URL, relevant heading, and source or evidence. Do not
    send supplier bank details, identity documents, product secrets, personal data, or other
    confidential files through a general contact channel.
  </p>

  <h2>Editorial boundaries</h2>
  <p>
    Havemoon cannot confirm product compliance, customs classification, legal status, supplier
    legitimacy, or shipment instructions from a short message. Those decisions require
    transaction-specific evidence and appropriately qualified professionals.
  </p>
</TrustPage>
